-- AC-5 ทุก refund ลง ledger แบบ double-entry ผลรวมต้องเป็นศูนย์
+- AC-5 (revised 2026-10-03, bd-104; supersedes the original, see Revision history) Every refund is posted to the ledger as double-entry. The sum of the entries may deviate from zero by at most 0.01 (inclusive, either sign, per post) to absorb upstream rounding; such a post still succeeds.
+  - Given a post with at least two entries whose sum is exactly 0, When `post()` runs, Then it posts and reports residual `0.0`.
+  - Given a sum of exactly +0.01 or exactly -0.01, When `post()` runs, Then it posts and the reported `amount` is the true residual (0.01 / -0.01), never zeroed or clamped.
+  - Given a sum whose absolute value exceeds 0.01 (e.g. +/-0.0100001, or -1000.00), When `post()` runs, Then it raises `ValueError("unbalanced")`.
+  - Given a post with a non-zero residual, When it is posted, Then one audit log line records the entry count and the residual, and it never contains the card number (PAN).
+  - Given any amount or total that is NaN or Infinity, When `post()` runs, Then it raises `ValueError` (not `decimal.InvalidOperation`) and never posts.
+  - Given a single non-zero entry (one-sided post), When `post()` runs, Then it is rejected; the tolerance applies only to multi-entry posts (default pending Q-4).
+  - Constraints: the 0.01 tolerance is a fixed named constant, not caller-, env- or entry-configurable; it is evaluated per post with exact Decimal arithmetic (no float); cumulative drift must be bounded or monitored (Q-3). Detail: `outputs/bd-104/01-security-engineer-phase-1c.md` S1-S10.
+  - Assumption (OPEN, unconfirmed): 0.01 means a 2-decimal currency. The repo has no currency field, so this is not verified. A fixed 0.01 is wrong for zero- or three-decimal currencies. Owner: user/Bella.
 
 ## Out of scope
 partial refund หลายครั้งต่อ order · การคืนเงินข้าม currency
+
+## Revision history
+- 2026-10-03 · bd-104 · AC-5 revised (AC-1..AC-4 unchanged).
+  - Original AC-5: "ทุก refund ลง ledger แบบ double-entry ผลรวมต้องเป็นศูนย์" (every refund posts double-entry; the sum must be zero).
+  - Reason: the user requested that `post()` accept a sum within 0.01 of zero because of upstream rounding. Source: bd-104 request; constraints from `outputs/bd-104/01-security-engineer-phase-1c.md`.
+  - Scope note: `post()` is in `src/ledger.py` and has no refund-specific logic, so the relaxation applies to every ledger post, not only refunds (Q-1 in the Phase 1c file).
+
+## Open questions (bd-104; user unavailable, not asked)
+- OQ-1 Currency: 0.01 assumes a 2-decimal currency; the repo has no currency field. Confirm the currency scope or whether the tolerance must scale per currency. Owner: user.
+- OQ-2 Residual destination (Phase 1c Q-3): rounding/suspense balancing entry vs monitoring counter only. The repo has no persistence layer; if unresolved, the gap is recorded as accepted risk, not a silent pass. Owner: user/Oliver.
+- OQ-3 One-sided and empty posts (Q-4): default is to reject a single non-zero entry and leave `post([])` unchanged. Owner: user/Bella.
+- OQ-4 Response shape (Q-2): whether to add an exact string `residual` next to the float `amount`. Default: no. Owner: user.
+- OQ-5 Scope (Q-1): confirm that relaxing for all ledger posts, not only refunds, is intended. Owner: user.
+- Out of this AC: pre-existing finding F-1 (full PAN printed to stdout) is tracked separately (Q-5).
